{"authored" [{"question" "q-65612" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{48}^{∘}}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{24}^{∘}}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/state.json" "file_sha256" "b46464c2c428587f418d4dd6e2f1ae99dc97713d6a5712ceed3e9b142d3456d1" "basis" 1288 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-65612" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={24}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {24}^{∘})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{24}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{24}^{∘}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{48}^{∘}=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{24}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{24}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nDividing both sides by $2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{24}^{∘},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{48}^{∘}}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{24}^{∘}} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{24}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{24}^{∘}}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{24}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{24}^{∘}\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{24}^{∘}}}{\\cancel{2}\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{24}^{∘}}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡{24}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/state.json" "file_sha256" "b46464c2c428587f418d4dd6e2f1ae99dc97713d6a5712ceed3e9b142d3456d1" "basis" 1288 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037917/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-65612" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma