 "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{48}^{∘}}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{24}^{∘}}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-65612" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={24}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {24}^{∘})=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{24}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{24}^{∘}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{48}^{∘}=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{24}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{24}^{∘}.\n$$\n\nDividing both sides by $2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{24}^{∘},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{48}^{∘}}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{24}^{∘}} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{24}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{24}^{∘}}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{24}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{24}^{∘}\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{24}^{∘}}}{\\cancel{2}\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{24}^{∘}}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡{24}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-65612" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8a4c559e4250e9365f60e8c5d7fae5ec914e88942bce73a2ac8ce107b5dac40d"} {"question" "q-65612" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-65612" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{24}^{∘}"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{tan}⁡{24}^{∘}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{48}^{∘}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡{24}^{∘}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{tan}⁡{48}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-65612" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{sin}⁡{24}^{∘}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-77893" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the line $2x-y-4=0$ and linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the equation of the image of the line under the action of $T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-77893" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that the line $2x-y-4=0$ passes through the points $R(0,-4)$ and $S(1,-2)$ since the coordinates of both points satisfy the equation.\n\nTo find the image of $R$ and $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing the coordinates of the points:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 3 \\\\ -12 & -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective image points are ${R}^{′}(8,-12)$ and ${S}^{′}(3,-6).$\n\nFinally, we write the equation of the line that passes through ${R}^{′}$ and ${S}^{′}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-{y}_{1} & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}}(x-{x}_{1}) \\\\ y-(-12) & =\\frac{-6-(-12)}{3-8}(x-8) \\\\ y+12 & =-\\frac{6}{5}(x-8) \\\\ 5y+60 & =-6x+48 \\\\ 6x+5y+12 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-77893" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8a4c559e4250e9365f60e8c5d7fae5ec914e88942bce73a2ac8ce107b5dac40d"} {"question" "q-77893" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-77893" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "5x+6y-12=0"] ["math" "5x-6y+12=0"] ["math" "5x-6y-2=0"] ["math" "6x+5y+12=0"] ["math" "6x-5y+12=0"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-77893" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6x+5y+12=0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-337668" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the product $AB$, if\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]$\nand \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & \\sqrt{3} & 5 \\\\ 4\\sqrt{2} & -1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & -3\\sqrt{5} & 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n| $AB=$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-337668" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $A$ is the $2$nd *row* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $B$ by the $2$nd *row* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}$ on the *left*, the result must be the $2$nd *row* of $B.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nAB=[\\begin{aligned}4\\sqrt{2} & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nLet's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & \\sqrt{3} & 5 \\\\ 4\\sqrt{2} & -1 & 0 \\\\ 7 & -3\\sqrt{5} & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4\\sqrt{2} & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-337668" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8a4c559e4250e9365f60e8c5d7fae5ec914e88942bce73a2ac8ce107b5dac40d"} {"question" "q-337668" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-337668" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-337668" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-337668" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-337668" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-337668" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-47675" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/assets/dd8697532367aa85a521d4af3af6f9184e89964f2619ee4dc4ffe84d21877f31.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ whose graph is plotted above. At which points is the function $f(x)$ **not** differentiable?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-47675" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The function is not differentiable wherever it has a discontinuity, corner, cusp, or vertical tangent.\n\n- At $x=-4$ the function has a jump discontinuity, so it's not differentiable there.\n\n- At $x=0$ the function has a corner, so it's not differentiable there.\n\n- At $x=4$ the function has an infinite discontinuity, so it's not differentiable there.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x=-4$, $x=0$, and $x=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-47675" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8a4c559e4250e9365f60e8c5d7fae5ec914e88942bce73a2ac8ce107b5dac40d"} {"question" "q-47675" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-47675" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$x=-4$ and $x=4$ only"] ["text" "$x=-4$ only"] ["text" "$x=-4$, $x=0$ and $x=4$"] ["text" "$x=0$ only"] ["text" "$x=4$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-47675" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$x=-4$, $x=0$ and $x=4$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-123699" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the limit of the sequence ${a}_{n}=\\frac{{n}^{2}}{{e}^{n/2}}-1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-123699" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that for large values of $n,$ we have\n\n$$\nn!≫{e}^{n}≫{n}^{m}≫\\operatorname{ln}⁡(n),\n$$\n\nwhere $≫$ means \"much greater than,\" and $m>0.$\n\nWe calculate the limit of the sequence as $n$ approaches infinity:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n}={lim}_{n\\to \\infty }(\\frac{{n}^{2}}{{e}^{n/2}}-1)=-1+{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{{n}^{2}}{{e}^{n/2}}\n$$\n\nBoth the numerator and denominator approach infinity as $n\\to \\infty .$ However, the denominator is growing much faster than the numerator, and we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{{n}^{2}}{{e}^{n/2}}=0.\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }{a}_{n}=-1+{lim}_{n\\to \\infty }\\frac{{n}^{2}}{{e}^{n/2}}=-1+0=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sequence converges and its limit is $-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-123699" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8a4c559e4250e9365f60e8c5d7fae5ec914e88942bce73a2ac8ce107b5dac40d"} {"question" "q-123699" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-123699" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["text" "The sequence diverges."]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-123699" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-70781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following values is in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-70781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/assets/d7984b9098d02bfc2b1e9a422aef919533abce54fbb94117e709c7613b0870a3.png)\n\nNote that:\n\n- The range of the function is $y\\in (-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$\n\nTherefore, of the given values, only $y=1$ is in the range of the function." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-70781" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8a4c559e4250e9365f60e8c5d7fae5ec914e88942bce73a2ac8ce107b5dac40d"} {"question" "q-70781" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-70781" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2\\pi "] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "\\pi "]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-70781" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-282168" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The quadratic polynomial $f(y)$ has real coefficients, has roots ${y}_{1}=2+3\\text{i}$ and ${y}_{2}=2-3\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $5.$ Find $f(y).$\n\n$f(y)=$ {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-282168" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${y}_{1}=2+3\\text{i}$ and ${y}_{2}=2-3\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=5,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(y-{y}_{1})(y-{y}_{2}) & =(5)(y-(2+3\\text{i}))(y-(2-3\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(y-(2+3\\text{i}))(y-(2-3\\text{i})) & =5({y}^{2}-(2+3\\text{i})y-(2-3\\text{i})y+(2+3\\text{i})(2-3\\text{i})) \\\\  & =5({y}^{2}-(2+3\\text{i}+2-3\\text{i})y+({2}^{2}-(3\\text{i})^{2})) \\\\  & =5({y}^{2}-4y+(4+9)) \\\\  & =5({y}^{2}-4y+13) \\\\  & =5{y}^{2}-20y+65.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(y)=5{y}^{2}-20y+65.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-282168" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8a4c559e4250e9365f60e8c5d7fae5ec914e88942bce73a2ac8ce107b5dac40d"} {"question" "q-282168" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-282168" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5y^2-20y+65"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-69940" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\text{u}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $\\text{v}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-69940" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot 2-2\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-2+2 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,0\\,|=0\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-69940" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8a4c559e4250e9365f60e8c5d7fae5ec914e88942bce73a2ac8ce107b5dac40d"} {"question" "q-69940" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-69940" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-69940" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-69563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}=1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-69563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=4$ and ${b}^{2}=49.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=4,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{4}=2.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=49,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{49}=7.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=7,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=2.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 7=14,$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 2=4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-69563" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8a4c559e4250e9365f60e8c5d7fae5ec914e88942bce73a2ac8ce107b5dac40d"} {"question" "q-69563" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-69563" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$14$ and $4$"] ["text" "$14\\sqrt{2}$ and $4\\sqrt{2}$"] ["text" "$7$ and $2$"] ["text" "$7$ and $4$"] ["text" "$7\\sqrt{2}$ and $2\\sqrt{2}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"} {"question" "q-69563" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "$14$ and $4$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041922/state.json" "file_sha256" "04625f8882fc4a05f05b888194b00dd192aab950acbe70588cc61fa2f5749bac"}] "usage" {"q-65612" []} "basis" 1546 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186298093 17592186298094 17592186298095 17592186298096 17592186298097] "immutable_fields" [[17592186298092 :answer-field/correct] [17592186298092 :answer-field/id] [17592186298092 :answer-field/key] [17